    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.trailspace\n\n### Description\n\nWhen working with tab-indented files, normally spaces preceding tabs are wrong. It would be useful to have them highlighted the same way of trailing spaces.\n\nSee also the `show_spaces_that_precede_tabs` option in https://github.com/ntpeters/vim-better-whitespace.\n\nThanks!",
